From a318bcc57f3da209d0b402c00804c719378f14bc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <claude@buttzeppelin>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 11:41:53 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Zeppelin F-223: ZepModernAdt 4-bit alpha, MH2O normalisation,
 async companions

- alpha follows the live map: RLE/8-bit pass through or 4-bit expands on big-alpha maps;
  every layer decodes and quantises to 2048 bytes on 4-bit maps (stock Outland)
- MH2O normalised as wxl-modern-adt does (placement-object redirect table, vertex format,
  out-of-range offsets, unusable liquid types fall back to water/magma)
- _tex0/_obj0 queued on the async file service ahead of the root (priority 125)
- MCNR always written as the 448 bytes ProcessIffChunks steps over (a 435-byte root
  shifted every later sub-chunk and lost MCRF: null ref list crash in CreateRefs)

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01ByrZ7GxoHC9wfGdkRwtqCX
---
